00:10:39.238 --> 00:10:41.106
You're not better than me,
Fauci.

00:10:41.106 --> 00:10:42.474
I'm just joking,
you make me laugh.

00:10:42.474 --> 00:10:44.310
You're my best friend."

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:46.912
So Trump fired off a random
tweet about Harry and Meghan,

00:10:46.912 --> 00:10:49.115
and yet it's not even remotely
the worst thing he tweeted

00:10:49.115 --> 00:10:51.316
this weekend because
he also bragged

00:10:51.316 --> 00:10:55.821
about the ratings for his press
conferences during the pandemic.

00:10:55.821 --> 00:10:58.290
"Because the 'ratings' of my
news conferences are so high,

00:10:58.290 --> 00:10:59.791
'"Bachelor' finale,"
"Monday Night Football"

00:10:59.791 --> 00:11:01.860
type numbers,' according
to "The New York Times,"

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:03.862
the Lamestream Media
is going crazy."

00:11:03.862 --> 00:11:05.163
And then later he tweeted,

00:11:05.163 --> 00:11:07.366
"President Trump
is a ratings hit."

00:11:07.366 --> 00:11:11.270
You're comparing your pandemic
briefings to "The Bachelor"?

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:14.239
Because at this point, I would
rather go to Peter's mom Barb

00:11:14.239 --> 00:11:16.141
for coronavirus updates.

00:11:16.141 --> 00:11:18.210
"All I know is after she showed
up three hours late

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:19.578
to our meeting in Australia,

00:11:19.578 --> 00:11:22.614
Madi needs to socially distance
herself from my son."

00:11:22.614 --> 00:11:25.384
I don't watch "The Bachelor,"
so I don't get that joke.

00:11:25.384 --> 00:11:27.386
Also I'm not saying it to say
I'm better than you.

00:11:27.386 --> 00:11:30.289
I mainlined "Love Is Blind"
in two nights, and, guys,

00:11:30.289 --> 00:11:33.992
when this is over, we need
to talk about Jessica

00:11:33.992 --> 00:11:37.429
because she's a real
Judge Jeanine.

00:11:37.429 --> 00:11:40.265
Also, people aren't tuning in
because they all love you.

00:11:40.265 --> 00:11:42.301
They're tuning in because
they're trapped inside

00:11:42.301 --> 00:11:44.002
and their only choices are
watching you

00:11:44.002 --> 00:11:46.272
or digging through Netflix
trying to find

00:11:46.272 --> 00:11:48.040
a British crime show
they haven't seen yet.

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:51.710
"Honey? Honey, did we watch
'Inspector Pinderberry'?"

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:54.747
"Yeah, remember?
The killer was the lorry driver

00:11:54.747 --> 00:11:56.648
and Pinderberry caught him
burying the body

00:11:56.648 --> 00:11:58.016
in the Yorkshire Moors?"

00:11:58.016 --> 00:11:59.852
"Ha, ha, that's right.

00:11:59.852 --> 00:12:04.489
No one outsmarts
Inspector Pinderberry."

00:12:04.489 --> 00:12:06.992
Also, we're only trapped
inside watching you

00:12:06.992 --> 00:12:08.760
because you kept ignoring
the crisis and pretending

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:10.930
it would go away
until it was too late.

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:13.098
We're forced to stay inside
and watch you

00:12:13.098 --> 00:12:15.233
because you screwed up.

00:12:15.233 --> 00:12:17.603
More people than ever are
playing Scrabble right now,

00:12:17.603 --> 00:12:21.006
but it sure as hell isn't
because Scrabble is fun.

00:12:21.006 --> 00:12:24.009
"Monday Night Football"
could score huge ratings too

00:12:24.009 --> 00:12:25.377
if every week they released

00:12:25.377 --> 00:12:28.246
millions of large exotic
wildcats onto the streets

00:12:28.246 --> 00:12:31.083
